{
  // Type-check-only project. It exists because `tsconfig.json` is the BUILD
  // config (`npm run build` is a bare `tsc`, which emits to ./dist), so the
  // exclusion of the test globs over there is load-bearing: dropping it would
  // ship the whole suite inside dist/.
  //
  // This project sets `noEmit`, so it can include everything the build leaves
  // out: the tests, the one-off scripts and the Prisma seed. Vitest does NOT
  // type-check, so without this command a test can reference a field that does
  // not exist, pass at runtime because the value is `undefined`, and nothing
  // ever complains.
  //
  // Run it with `npm run typecheck:tests`. See section 7 of
  // docs/superpowers/workout-start-race-STATUS.md.
  //
  // NOTE: line comments only. A block comment holding a glob like the test
  // pattern closes itself early on the `*` + `/` inside it, and tsc parses the
  // wreckage WITHOUT complaining -- it just silently builds another config.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    // The build pins `rootDir` to ./src because that is what shapes ./dist.
    // Here nothing is emitted, and src/__tests__/import-off-foods.test.ts
    // imports from ../../scripts/, so the root has to be the package.
    "rootDir": "."
  },
  "include": [
    "src/**/*",
    "scripts/**/*",
    "prisma/**/*"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist"
  ]
}
